### 2. Project Card (`components/ProjectCard.tsx`)
- A modular card component for the grid.
- **Styling Rules:** 
  - Dark background (e.g., `bg-slate-900` or `bg-[#0d1117]`) with a subtle border.
  - Project title in a terminal-style accent color (e.g., green or cyan).
  - Tags must be rendered at the bottom as pill-shaped terminal badges (e.g., `[ Python ]`).
- **Strict Rule:** Do not include any GitHub links or GitHub icons beside the projects.

### 3. Project Grid & Filtering (`components/ProjectGrid.tsx`)
- Renders the `ProjectCard` components in a responsive grid (1 column on mobile, 2 or 3 on desktop).
- Include a simple interactive filter mechanism at the top (e.g., "All", "Python", "React", "Jenkins") to filter projects by tag.
- **Animations:** Use Framer Motion's `staggerChildren` and `whileInView` so the cards cascade into view sequentially as the user scrolls.

### 4. Dynamic Project Page (`app/projects/[slug]/page.tsx`)
- Set up a Next.js dynamic route to display extended details for a single project based on its `slug`.
- The layout should mimic opening a detailed markdown file in a code editor (e.g., showing the title as `[slug].md`).
- Add a "cd .." or "<- Back to projects" link styled as a terminal command to return to the main page.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Next.js app compiles and runs with zero errors (`npm run dev`).
- [ ] `ProjectGrid.tsx` successfully maps and renders data from `content/projects.ts`.
- [ ] No GitHub links or icons are present on the project cards.
- [ ] The tag filtering system correctly updates the visible projects.
- [ ] Clicking a project card successfully routes the user to `app/projects/[slug]`.
- [ ] Project cards animate smoothly into view upon scrolling.